 "best_diff": "--- initial\n+++ best\n@@ -19,7 +19,26 @@\n     features (they are standardized and a bias is added), so nonlinear structure only\n     helps if a feature expresses it. Only the Python standard library may be used.\n \n-    Current method: the raw inputs.\n+    Current method: log + interactions + radii.\n     \"\"\"\n-    return list(row)\n+    x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6 = row\n+    features = []\n+    # Raw features\n+    features.extend(row)\n+    # Log transform for skewed positive input x3\n+    features.append(math.log(x3))\n+    # Pairwise interaction products\n+    features.append(x1 * x2)\n+    features.append(x1 * x3)\n+    features.append(x2 * x3)\n+    features.append(x4 * x5)\n+    # Radial features for circular/quadratic patterns\n+    features.append(x1*x1 + x2*x2)\n+    features.append(x4*x4 + x5*x5)\n+    # Sign features for quadrant patterns\n+    s12 = x1 * x2\n+    s45 = x4 * x5\n+    features.append(math.copysign(1.0, s12) if s12 != 0 else 0.0)\n+    features.append(math.copysign(1.0, s45) if s45 != 0 else 0.0)\n+    return features\n # OMEGA-BLOCK-END\n",
